<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<subsection xml:id="ch9-section-isobaric-coordinates-subsection-mass-conservation" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
    <title>Mass conservation</title>

    <p>
        Returning to the statement of mass conservation for an air parcel from
        <xref ref="ch6-section-lagrangian" text="custom">Chapter 6</xref>:
    </p>

    <p>
        <md xml:id="eqn-mass-conservation-reproduced" number="yes">
            \frac{Dm}{D t} = 0
        </md>
    </p>

    <p>
        Recall this statement means the air parcel of interest does not exchange mass with its environment.
    </p>

    <p>
        The air parcel's mass is given by
    </p>
    
    <p>
        <md number="yes">
            m = \rho V
        </md>
    </p>

    <p>
        and as we have done since <xref ref="chapter-3" text="type-global" />,
        we assume the air parcel is a rectangular prism with length <m>\delta x</m>, width <m>\delta y</m>, and height <m>\delta z</m>,
        so its volume is
    </p>
        
    <p>
        <md number="yes">
            V = \delta x \, \delta y \, \delta z
        </md>
    </p>
    
    <p>
        But now that we are using <m>p</m> rather than <m>z</m> as the vertical coordinate and have the hydrostatic approximation at our disposal,
        we can rearrange the mathematical equation of hydrostatic balance to solve for <m>\delta z</m>
    </p>

    <p>
        <md number="yes">
            \delta z= - \frac{\delta p}{\rho g}
        </md>
    </p>

    <p>
        and then we can substitute this expression into <m>V</m>:
    </p>

    <p>
        <md number="yes">
            V
            =
            \delta x \, \delta y \, \delta z
            =
            \delta x \, \delta y \left( -\frac{\delta p}{\rho g} \right)
            =
            -\frac{\delta x \, \delta y \, \delta p}{\rho g}
        </md>
    </p>

    <p>
        Then
    </p>

    <p>
        <md number="yes">
            m
            =
            \rho V
            =
            \rho \left( -\frac{\delta x \, \delta y \, \delta p}{\rho g} \right)
            =
            -\frac{\delta x \, \delta y \, \delta p}{g}
        </md>
    </p>

    <p>
        If we neglect variations in <m>g</m> by assuming changes in <m>z</m> are small,
        we can treat <m>g</m> as a constant and write the statement of mass conservation for an air parcel as
    </p>

    <p>
        <md xml:id="eqn-mass-conservation-isobaric-start" number="yes">
            \frac{D m}{Dt}
            =
            -\frac{1}{g}\frac{D \left( \delta x \, \delta y \, \delta p \right)}{Dt}
            =
            0
        </md>
    </p>

    <p>
        We expand <xref ref="eqn-mass-conservation-isobaric-start" text="type-global" /> by applying the product rule:
    </p>

    <p>
        <md>
            <mrow>
                \frac{Dm}{Dt}
                \amp =
                -\frac{1}{g}\frac{D \left( \delta x \, \delta y \, \delta p \right)}{Dt}
            </mrow>
            <mrow>
                \amp =
                -\frac{1}{g}
                \left[
                    \delta y \, \delta p \frac{D \delta x}{Dt}
                    + 
                    \delta x \, \delta p \frac{D \delta y}{Dt}
                    +
                    \delta x \, \delta y \frac{D \delta p}{Dt}
                \right]
            </mrow>
            <mrow number="yes">
                \amp = 0
            </mrow>
        </md>
    </p>

    <p>
        Since <m>\dfrac{D \delta x}{Dt} = \delta u</m>,
        <m>\dfrac{D \delta y}{Dt} = \delta v</m>,
        and <m>\dfrac{D \delta p}{Dt} = \delta \omega</m>,
        we have
    </p>

    <p>
        <md xml:id="eqn-mass-conservation-isobaric-intermediate" number="yes">
            \frac{Dm}{Dt}
            =
            -\frac{1}{g}
            \left[
                \delta y \, \delta p \, \delta u
                +
                \delta x \, \delta p \, \delta v
                +
                \delta x \, \delta y \, \delta \omega
            \right]
            = 0
        </md>
    </p>

    <p>
        Dividing <xref ref="eqn-mass-conservation-isobaric-intermediate" text="type-global" />
        by <m>m = -\dfrac{\delta x \, \delta y \, \delta p}{g}</m> produces
    </p>

</subsection>